 "observations": [
  "body L1, L6, L31: the dashes of the letter-spaced «al–Battānī» are long dashes (4.8 to 5.5 pt).",
  "body L2-L30: the minus signs are printed as long dashes (8.6 to 10.6 pt); they are set as minus signs.",
  "body L7-L8: rule (γ) is Ptolemy's theorem in the symmetric quadrilateral of the two stars and the points of the same latitudes at the other longitude: the product of the chords of the two longitudinal sides, with the square of the chord of β − β′ added, is the square of the chord of the distance.",
  "body L11-L21: the steps are right: L13 is L11 divided by 4, with sin² x/2 = (R² − R cos x)/2; L16 is twice L14 divided by R; with cos (β − β′) of L17 the terms cos β cos β′/R cancel, which gives L19, and with R = 1 L21.",
  "body L24-L25: with Δ = 90° − β and Δ′ = 90° − β′ the formula is that of the triangle FDE, with the sides FD = Δ and FE = Δ′ and the angle L − L′ at the pole F of the ecliptic.",
  "body L27: the dash after «IV.» measures 9.7 pt; transcribed as a dash.",
  "body L28-L30: the formula of case IV is right: with β + β′ in place of β − β′, cos (β + β′) = (cos β cos β′ − sin β sin β′)/R, and the term sin β sin β′/R changes its sign.",
  "body L31: a period stands after «Günther», where a comma would introduce the title.",
  "body L32-L33: the dash of the years 1877–79 is printed at the end of L32 (5.5 pt) and again at the head of L33.",
  "notes_left L2: the dash of «1890–93» is a long dash (4.3 pt in the type of the notes).",
  "notes_right L1: the dash of «416-417» measures 3.4 pt, as a hyphen.",
  "notes_right L2: the dash before «Amirucius» measures 7.9 pt."
 ],
